# Line endings for the files Linux consumes at runtime.
#
# Most developers here are on Windows with core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites
# checked-out files to CRLF. Harmless for source, but it breaks these:
#
#   api/container/startup.sh   copied into the image and run as the container
#                              ENTRYPOINT. With CRLF, `sh /app/startup.sh`
#                              fails on line 1 with $'\r': command not found
#                              and the container never starts.
#   .azure/env/*.env           sourced by bash in the pipeline. With CRLF every
#                              value gets a trailing \r, so the web app name
#                              becomes "cmms\r" and every az call fails.
#   api/container/sshd_config  read by sshd inside the image.
#   api/Dockerfile             RUN lines are executed by a shell in the image.
#
# Deliberately scoped to our own files rather than a repo-wide `* text=auto`:
# this is a downstream fork, and a blanket rule renormalises upstream files
# (mobile/android/gradlew.bat and friends), which is 100+ lines of pure
# line-ending churn to re-resolve on every upstream merge. See CLAUDE.md.

api/container/startup.sh    text eol=lf
api/container/sshd_config   text eol=lf
api/Dockerfile              text eol=lf
.azure/env/*.env            text eol=lf
